From 046a0cb4ab4b3935025e9b3e3ec316474c4ffebe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 22:57:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04555/11362] [outer-loop] GAP-4891 attempt: richer-scalar
 goal-energy BUILT + REFUTED -> the gap is RELATIONAL, not scalar

Operator "tackle GAP-4891 next". Built induce_goal_energy_richer (arc_agi3_goal_induction.py):
a value/fill/spatial scalar ladder (nonbg_cells, max_color_count, nonbg_bbox_area,
color_entropy) under the same strict-separation anti-mis-induction guard as the GAP-4890
single-positive operator, drop-in for the graph_explore_solve_v2 goal_energy hook. 3 new unit
tests pass (test_arc_single_positive_goal_energy.py; 7 total).

EMPIRICAL RESULT (the honest finding): re-ran the stage-1.6 probe on all 4 grid-based stalled
games (cd82/sk48/sp80/cn04) -- the richer SCALAR operator STILL returns None
(operator_used=None, separating_feature=None; adversarial_verify clean 4/4). ROOT CAUSE: the
negatives include NEAR-WIN frames (the penultimate frame differs from the win by ~one cell), so
NO global scalar -- count, fill, OR spatial-extent -- can strictly separate the win. The goal is
RELATIONAL/CELL-LEVEL (the configuration matches a within-frame TARGET; win vs penultimate differ
only in specific cell VALUES), which no global statistic expresses.

So GAP-4891 is re-scoped: global scalars are now EMPIRICALLY RULED OUT; the missing feature is a
WITHIN-FRAME RELATIONAL TARGET-MATCH (induce a region-pair equal-in-win-not-in-negatives -> Hamming
mismatch energy; re-read the target per level so it generalises). The richer operator stays (reusable
for any game whose goal IS scalar-separable). This is layered negative progress: counts (GAP-4890) ->
scalars (this) -> relational (next), each empirically narrowing the design. Confirmed binding: .451 A2
level-up just stalled (repro=False) on exactly this class.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
